OL,3,AAugust joint-hottest month on record as
OL,4,Aclimate change and El Nino drive heat
OL,5,
OL,6,FAugust was the joint-hottest month ever
OL,7,Frecorded, tying with July 2023,
OL,8,Faccording to the EU's climate service.
OL,10,FThe record was driven by a combination
OL,11,Fof climate change and the rising
OL,12,Finfluence of El Nino, pushing heat into
OL,13,Fthe atmosphere across the Pacific.
OL,15,FTemperatures for the month were 1.65C
OL,16,Fabove pre-industrial levels -
OL,17,Fsurpassing the critical 1.5C threshold
OL,18,Fagreed by countries to avoid the worst
OL,19,Fconsequences of climate change.
OL,23,APub: 10-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
